## Summary

Part of #63 (Hunter). The empty `content/skills/hunter` module and its pack, so that the hunter content PRs that follow (bird snares and box traps, bird houses, butterflies, Herbiboar, implings, Hunters' Rumours) can each add to the same new module without any two of them conflicting. This follows the "one PR per row" split you asked for in #353.

- `content/skills/hunter/build.gradle.kts`: the module, with `api/plugin-commons`, `api/utils/utils-skills` and `content/quest` as dependencies (the same three for its `integration` test suite).
- `content/skills/hunter/pack/build.gradle.kts`: the pack module, with `engine/map`.
- The two `gamevals.toml` files (`src/main/resources` with `dbtable`, `dbrow` and `timer` sections; `pack/src/main/resources` with `varp`), each section holding one anchor comment per feature (`# implings`, `# bird houses`, `# traps`, `# herbiboar`, `# butterflies`, `# rumours`). Each feature PR adds its ids under its own anchor, so they merge in any order.

This commit adds no content and no gameval ids; it is the base for the hunter PRs. Each of those names this branch as its dependency.

